    "title": "Learn a communication strategy",
    "subtitle": "How long things last · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the reference vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U17. Discuss duration and continuing situations; extend common verb-object expressions.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U17-skill-K-HSK2-interact-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 2: interact",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Ask about the partner’s actual experience and use their answer in the next turn. If you miss a part, request repetition before drawing a conclusion.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "见面",
                "pinyin": "jiànmiàn",
                "meaning": "to meet; to see each other",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "dd1a460a219ad94029dd26e7cde944b63511cfb98b4f9b440710f30e361c30f4"
              },
              {
                "text": "以前",
                "pinyin": "yǐqián",
                "meaning": "before; formerly",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "23ef8698ece36f71061b7f8b95e7534ecd3e0cafd553e9b1d62dd755854aee6c"
              },
              {
                "text": "请再说一遍",
                "pinyin": "qǐngzàishuōyībiàn",
                "meaning": "please say it once more",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "d067378704cc216bbf96aa487b12844cc687e51a9f702cca94f1f73fa0921d5e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "You are arranging a meeting. The partner says they have visited Beijing before, but you miss whether they want to meet today or tomorrow. Ask about their experience, request repetition of the missed meeting time, then propose meeting after that time is clarified. Do not invent their answer.\nFamiliar meanings available: to meet; to see each other; before; formerly; please say it once more."
          }
        ]
      },
